{"name":"Petrichor","hex":"#66cccc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"petrichor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The distinctive scent, caused by geosmin, which accompanies the first rain after a long, warm, dry spell.","The yellow organic oil that yields this scent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petrichor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Petrichor","blocks":[{"text":"Petrichor is the earthy scent often associated with rain falling on dry soil or rock. The term was introduced by Australian researchers Isabel Joy Bear and Richard Grenfell Thomas in a 1964 paper in Nature. Bear and Thomas used the term for an odour released from rock or soil materials after dry conditions when they are exposed to moisture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Water_and_soil_splashed_by_the_impact_of_a_single_raindrop.jpg/330px-Water_and_soil_splashed_by_the_impact_of_a_single_raindrop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrichor","wikidata":"Q1787101"},{"title":"Petrichor (composition)","blocks":[{"text":"Petrichor is an orchestral composition written by the American composer Ellen Reid. The work was commissioned by the Los Angeles Chamber Orchestra. Its world premiere was performed by the Los Angeles Chamber Orchestra conducted by Douglas Boyd at the UCLA's Royce Hall on February 24, 2018."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Ellen_Reid%2C_Composer_and_Sound_Artist.jpg/330px-Ellen_Reid%2C_Composer_and_Sound_Artist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petrichor_(composition)","wikidata":"Q121046478"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Water_drop_on_leaf_%2821880%29.jpg/500px-Water_drop_on_leaf_%2821880%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Water_drop_on_leaf_%2821880%29.jpg/1280px-Water_drop_on_leaf_%2821880%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Water_drop_on_leaf_%2821880%29.jpg/500px-Water_drop_on_leaf_%2821880%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Water drop on the leaf of a flowering plant after rain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_drop_on_leaf_(21880).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Leaf_with_droplets.jpg/500px-Leaf_with_droplets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Leaf_with_droplets.jpg/1280px-Leaf_with_droplets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Leaf_with_droplets.jpg/500px-Leaf_with_droplets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A leaf with droplets on damp soil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeaf_with_droplets.jpg"}],"sounds":{"petrichor":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ae/En-ca-petrichor.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ae/En-ca-petrichor.ogg/En-ca-petrichor.ogg.mp3"}]}}}